				<title>A Cycling Trip To The Hoz e Sultan; A saltwater lake in central Iran (Photos)</title>
				<link>https://jadi.space/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 01 Dec 2021 09:50:42 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://jadi.space/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;picture&gt;&#xA;      &lt;source&#xA;        type=&#34;image/webp&#34;&#xA;        srcset=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/img-01_hu_68f35a4ea47846c1.webp 300w,/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/img-01_hu_8a2db359bcb22251.webp 500w,/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/img-01_hu_df956c23050fa54f.webp 700w&#34;&#xA;        sizes=&#34;(max-width: 499px) 300px,(max-width: 699px) 500px,700px&#34;&#xA;      /&gt;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xA;        src=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/img-01.jpeg&#34;&#xA;        srcset=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/img-01_hu_f8a3f148f5c1d32b.jpeg 300w,/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/img-01_hu_2a97699f2e890ffd.jpeg 500w,/blog/a-cycling-trip-to-the-hoz-e-sultan-a-saltwater-lake-in-central-iran-photos/img-01_hu_d21e617a73205569.jpeg 700w&#34;&#xA;        sizes=&#34;(max-width: 499px) 300px,(max-width: 699px) 500px,700px&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;Hoz Sultan&#34;&#xA;        &#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;        width=&#34;1080&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;810&#34;&#xA;      /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/picture&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;em&gt;Cycling in Iran deserts, Hoz Sultan saltwater lake&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hoz e Sultan (حوض سلطان / &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://goo.gl/maps/Uk6S7xRrJHYvrCoQA&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;    class=&#34;link--external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;&gt;google maps&lt;/a&gt;) which means “Sultans Pool” in Farsi is located 85 KM south of Tehran. It’s a saltwater lake in the middle of a desert so its dry during the summer and salt harvesters are busy exploiting it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But in this sunny late November weekend and after two weeks of rain we decided that its the best time to visit the place and it was indeed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>GitHub is limiting MANY accounts from Iran and I think its Over Acting</title>
				<link>https://jadi.space/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 28 Jul 2019 15:01:36 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://jadi.space/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UPDATE:&lt;/strong&gt; it seems rebuilding github.io sites, will bring them back online. thumbs up github&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It was a shock. Today I’ve got many mails telling me that “your book gives me 404 errors”. You know it; 404 is “page not found”. I have written and translated 4 books and some other projects using github pages. These are static sites and 404 should be impossible, but is it?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;picture&gt;&#xA;      &lt;source&#xA;        type=&#34;image/webp&#34;&#xA;        srcset=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/img-01_hu_afceacffc6f70306.webp 300w,/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/img-01_hu_b4de02507c303a60.webp 500w,/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/img-01_hu_6c87d4173bb53db7.webp 700w&#34;&#xA;        sizes=&#34;(max-width: 499px) 300px,(max-width: 699px) 500px,700px&#34;&#xA;      /&gt;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xA;        src=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/img-01.png&#34;&#xA;        srcset=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/img-01_hu_271cc1459953d2d3.png 300w,/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/img-01_hu_993fe018d8d52f9c.png 500w,/blog/github-is-limiting-many-accounts-from-iran-and-i-think-its-over-acting/img-01_hu_28e7859b1e6ced26.png 700w&#34;&#xA;        sizes=&#34;(max-width: 499px) 300px,(max-width: 699px) 500px,700px&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;This is happening for MANY people&#34;&#xA;        &#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;        width=&#34;1400&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;647&#34;&#xA;      /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/picture&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;em&gt;This is happening for MANY people&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Twitter is still blocked in Iran, on DNS level</title>
				<link>https://jadi.space/blog/twitter-is-still-blocked-in-iran-on-dns-level/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 17 Nov 2016 16:58:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://jadi.space/blog/twitter-is-still-blocked-in-iran-on-dns-level/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Twitter has a strange condition in Iran. It is blocked on our Filternet (that is how we call the Internet!) but at the same time many officials do have twitter accounts; including the Leader, the president, some of the ministers, some parliament members, Tehran’s municipality and many others. Last week one of the &lt;em&gt;reformist&lt;/em&gt; parliament members started tweeting about “why the Twitter is Blocked?” and asked followers to provide him some reasons on “why the state should unblock the twitter”. He claimed that he want to try his chance unblocking twitter!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>How to “hack” any Instagram account and maybe anyone on Facebook</title>
				<link>https://jadi.space/blog/how-to-hack-any-instagram-account-and-maybe-anyone-on-facebook/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 14 Nov 2016 17:44:35 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://jadi.space/blog/how-to-hack-any-instagram-account-and-maybe-anyone-on-facebook/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;During the last month there were some news about “hacked Instagram accounts” of various famous Iranians. By “famous” I mean Iranian-Cyber-Famous and not International-Hollywood-Famous. Among them one person with enough cyber cautiousness whom hopefully will not fall for normal phishing attacks. So&amp;hellip; the question is “how”? My friend Ahmad Takhtdar has an idea and I’m going to explain it to you.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There is a form on Instagram which lets you recover your hacked account. It is located at &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://help.instagram.com/contact/740949042640030&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;    class=&#34;link--external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;&gt;https://help.instagram.com/contact/740949042640030&lt;/a&gt;. Using this form you can claim a hacked account back even if you are not able to login into that account and you do not have access to the email used for sign up.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>If you are in #iBridges 2015, make sure not to miss these points</title>
				<link>https://jadi.space/blog/if-you-are-in-ibridge-2015-make-sure-not-to-miss-these-points/</link>
				<pubDate>Sat, 06 Jun 2015 08:27:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://jadi.space/blog/if-you-are-in-ibridge-2015-make-sure-not-to-miss-these-points/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;During last 3 days, iBridges conference was all over Iranian twitter and non-governmental media. Many of my friends were attending the conference and many were critisizing it of many different aspects.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://ibridges.org/&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;    class=&#34;link--external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&#xA;  &#xA;&gt;iBridges.org: Berlin, 4-6 June 2015&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In general I believe that having this conference is good thing since it presents Iranian tech industry to the international eyes and make Iran⇄World ties stronger which is a good news for us.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>I can not sync my kindle from Iran — anymore</title>
				<link>https://jadi.space/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 15 May 2015 06:27:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://jadi.space/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;I love my kindle… or… it is more accurate if I say I love reading books and my kindle is a great solution for this purpose. I live in Iran — one of the Internet blackholes and a county in which every single book which is going to be published, should be evaluated and certificated by the censors.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;  &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;      &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;          &#xA;        &#xA;      &#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;picture&gt;&#xA;      &lt;source&#xA;        type=&#34;image/webp&#34;&#xA;        srcset=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/img-01_hu_66f2ec21c0d54dba.webp 300w,/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/img-01_hu_553d9d3b09e3da54.webp 500w,/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/img-01_hu_964cc5245d25c4e3.webp 700w&#34;&#xA;        sizes=&#34;(max-width: 499px) 300px,(max-width: 699px) 500px,700px&#34;&#xA;      /&gt;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xA;        src=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/img-01.png&#34;&#xA;        srcset=&#34;https://jadi.space/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/img-01_hu_7ce20e6e3d407fb1.png 300w,/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/img-01_hu_375050de5417309c.png 500w,/blog/i-can-not-sync-my-kindle-from-iran-anymore/img-01_hu_6b028a4dd76419a8.png 700w&#34;&#xA;        sizes=&#34;(max-width: 499px) 300px,(max-width: 699px) 500px,700px&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;In Iran, censors change books, translations, poems, .. and every publication should have a license from the state and the ministry of Culture and Islamic Guidance&#34;&#xA;        &#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;        width=&#34;1000&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;650&#34;&#xA;      /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/picture&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;em&gt;In Iran, censors change books, translations, poems, .. and every publication should have a license from the state and the ministry of Culture and Islamic Guidance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
